 they  were infected with kova 19  caused more deaths and this report at  least preliminarily is saying  it looks that way and we're going to  continue to invest in indictment really  stunning stuff brian thank you quick  reporting on that brian yennis thank you  the governor was talking about this just  this week the governor  was on did an interview in which he said  it was federal incompetence  and incompetent government kills people  more people died than needed to die in  covet that's the truth well  indeed it is the other thing is remember  this governor wrote a book about how  well he did in a pandemic response it  got it became a bestseller  and then he won an emmy for his  briefings for briefings  and now you have families they weren't  there to be able to hold their loved  ones hands they weren't able to have a  funeral  and now they're finding this out what  brian's reporting at the end there is  important to emphasize  these were coveted patients who were  being treated at local hospitals here in  new york  and the order came out that said once  they're released from the hospital the  nursing home  must take them back in well these  nursing centers with all the elderly  they were the most vulnerable  of all at any point in covet 19  especially during march and april of  last year it's a really stunning  indictment where we've reached out to  the ag hopefully we get our honor very  soon we'd love to have her and  talk to him great show today thank you  for being here

